{
  "step_1": "The decision reason can be applied to the decision problem. The reason focuses on the least probable outcomes — specifically, the most favorable outcome with the lowest (minimum) probability in each lottery. For Lottery A: the outcomes are 4000 (25%), 2000 (25%), and 0 (50%). The most favorable outcome is 4000 Euros with a probability of 25%. For Lottery B: the outcomes are 6000 (25%) and 0 (75%). The most favorable outcome is 6000 Euros with a probability of 25%. Since both lotteries have their most favorable outcome at 25% probability, these are the least probable (and most favorable) outcomes for each. Comparing them: Lottery B has a more favorable least probable outcome (6000 > 4000). Therefore, the decision reason would prefer Lottery B.",
